{"title":"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/6/5a69ddf3e0a13f43f0701d55b1a554a4a8d29a11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4(\\heartsuit)^2 = 144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"21\" />, then a value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/c/38c6b4ac9e30aa1bbcdf4529130bc58e4b392e83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\heartsuit$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/2/e62874f4f9036b3da6bea3bfea9f425d6d82a872.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 3 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 6 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 9 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 12 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"406\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can just treat the heart as a variable like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/6/fb6221c87374c6be3b413c4856427c769f5d6c7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x^2 = 144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Dividing both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/5/925f1e07d18cdb29c5a156a1058e65d4531a560e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4x^2}{4} = x^2 = \\frac{144}{4} = 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"173\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>For this to be true, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/7/ea7da1b75cc1a945018db7316c26d618ca11ff9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c439b9dc606f5ca70f88a79d9f965c46a79ffdd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -6$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/9/8c988ebe5644e5aecf74986aa84a0f6fd8d4b261.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^2 = 6 \\times 6 = 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/2/f824a07fdfff6684c4dffa4af782ed5343da7b47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-6)^2 = -6 \\times -6 = 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"182\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Of these values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/d/f4dbc31d09b3d6ad5e17b7c49ab8e9da67588f38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"57\" height=\"30\" /> is an answer choice.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal\">1999 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Pro